@* One line of a list you pick from, with the mark that says which one is chosen. The row's
   chrome is .pick-row (see site.css — the class the three RowClass helpers collapsed into);
   this is the other half those call sites still spelled out separately: the button itself,
   the is-active state, and the trailing check — which had already drifted between `ml-auto`
   and `shrink-0` on rows that do the same job in three folders.

   What the row shows stays with the caller, since one lists people with avatars and another
   scope choices with badges. The check is pushed to the trailing edge whatever the content,
   so a row body needn't be flex-1 for the mark to land in the same place on every list. *@

@* focus-ring, as every button that is not a .btn wears — the rows had none, so three pickers
   answered the keyboard with nothing. aria-pressed says in words what the check says in ink. *@
<button type="button" class="pick-row focus-ring @(Active ? "is-active" : null)"
        aria-pressed="@Aria.Flag(Active)" @onclick="OnClick">
    @ChildContent
    @if (Active)
    {
        <Icon Name="check" Class="w-4 h-4 text-accent-700 ml-auto shrink-0"/>
    }
</button>

@code {
    /// <summary>Whether this row is the current pick — tints the row and draws the check.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Active { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnClick { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }
}
